        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitalliance.com/about-alliance/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was originally called Grand Lake before the railroad prompted a one‑word name change to Alliance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alliance%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Box Butte County earned its name from the distinctive box‑shaped buttes that rise above the surrounding sandhills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitalliance.com/about-alliance/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Nebraska Stock Growers Association, founded in Alliance in 1889, was created to protect stockmen from illegal rustling.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
